<p>Peru&#x27;s National Jury of Elections confirmed Sunday that Keiko Fujimori of Fuerza Popular and Roberto Sánchez of Juntos por el Perú will compete in a June 7 presidential runoff after neither candidate won more than half of valid votes in the April 12 first round. The official count put Fujimori first with 17.19% and Sánchez second with 12.03%, while ultraconservative Rafael López Aliaga finished third with 11.91%. The count took 33 days. The national election office completed 100% of tally-sheet processing before the JNE certified the results. The first round saw delays in the delivery of election materials in Lima, and some voting centers had to reopen the next day; Peru&#x27;s top electoral authority pledged to correct flaws before the runoff. Fujimori, 50, is the daughter of late former President Alberto Fujimori and is making her fourth presidential bid, while Sánchez, 57, is a former trade minister under former President Pedro Castillo.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/qHnlw5rq1fSR4KxFLjLCi2-XCD-VOFOW277AXC_fZXptACTSJQ2l921LfZ4DdSERPxlg4qBFfIW_t74odRJJnyWOiS6FTjpi3b-J8_k04dnSf1kPWjtnNvKWERTZd7R_nfrXvW6J3neBCfIW_oB6SlnzsmXtljkg0MYF19Ycfsw6saQzm8ni1S1m2kKkeOPIUbHVsNkFvGxlY1J9iLDYpOe-9Kr80Ug5kOXEcfKQY-2-LMCuLclZA4TpEFoPbzLLxLpKbTdyepHLjtZ-_AG57xTjxY_UOBU' alt='Roberto Sánchez and Keiko Fujimori will contest Peru&#x27;s presidential runoff.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Narrow margin: The second-place contest was decided by 21,209 votes, with Sánchez receiving 2,015,114 votes and López Aliaga receiving 1,993,905.</li><li>Mandate period: The JNE proclamation covered the presidential tickets seeking Peru&#x27;s 2026-2031 term.</li><li>Formal certification: Representatives of both Fujimori&#x27;s and Sánchez&#x27;s parties signed the official results at the JNE ceremony.</li><li>Complaint context: Delays were reported especially in Lima and in the United States, and elDiario.es said fraud complaints tied to those delays lacked conclusive evidence.</li></ul><blockquote>Hoje estão em risco a estabilidade econômica, a democracia, a liberdade para empreender e para trabalhar (…) convoco vocês a transformar o medo e a decepção em ação e em esperança - Keiko Fujimori</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Peru&#x27;s National Jury of Elections: The JNE said its decision confirming the two runoff candidates was final and could not be appealed. (<a href='https://www.aa.com.tr/en/americas/peru-s-election-authority-confirms-advancement-of-fujimori-sanchez-to-runoff/3940479'>Anadolu Agency</a>)</li><li>Rafael López Aliaga: López Aliaga refused to recognize the results and said on X that he would immediately challenge what he called a grave crime of treason, fraud and corruption. (<a href='https://jovempan.com.br/noticias/mundo/eleicao-no-peru-orgao-eleitoral-confirma-fujimori-e-sanchez-no-segundo-turno.html'>Jovem Pan</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/perus-electoral-board-confirms-june-7-presidential-runoff-133050906'>Peru&#x27;s electoral board confirms June 7 presidential runoff with Fujimori and Sánchez</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/5/17/peruvian-authorities-confirm-fujimori-and-sanchez-advance-to-runoff'>Peruvian authorities confirm Fujimori and Sanchez advance to runoff</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/peru-electoral-body-pledges-to-fix-voting-flaws-ahead-of-june-presidential-runoff'>Peru electoral body pledges to fix voting &#x27;flaws&#x27; ahead of June presidential runoff</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/perus-fujimori-and-sanchez-to-meet-in-june-7-presidential-runoff'>Peru&#x27;s Fujimori and Sánchez to meet in June 7 presidential runoff</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/05/18/g-s1-122536/peru-presidential-runoff'>Peru&#x27;s electoral board confirms June 7 presidential runoff</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='